  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    The Fire Keepers are a Nightshelf organization responsible for safeguarding fire-cores — the solidified volcanic heat-crystals that sustain life beneath the ice. Their mandate encompasses the maintenance, transport, and protection of these cores: tending the heating braziers that keep tunnels habitable, overseeing fire-core shipments bound for the surface markets under the Flipper Accord, and intervening when cores destabilize. The work is unglamorous. It is also the reason anyone in the deep tunnels is alive.
    
    ## Founding and Theology
    
    The Fire Keepers trace their lineage to Chill-breaker Sanctervilevia~ Ice, recorded in smoke-oaths as *she-who-entered-the-still-beating-chamber* — the first to touch the wall of the god's heart and feel it pulse. Their theological position holds that the Berg is a ward rather than a temple: the god sleeps rather than died, the tunnels follow paths divine blood carved before any shaper put flipper to stone, and fire-cores are clots of that blood too dense to freeze. This places them in direct opposition to the Wake-Singers' claim that a god was killed and the Aurora liturgists' account of willing transformation. All three traditions disagree on everything except the Omega Obelisk's inexplicability.
    
    The first fire-keepers, by this account, sealed the deep chambers from the inside — not against external intrusion but against the body's own spasms, its flesh remembering it was once alive. Their traditions are preserved in smoke-oath and tunnel-chant. What they locked within the god's body, they locked as custodians who understood the interior best.
    
    ## Techniques and Practice
    
    The oldest stabilization methods include pressure-chants and bone-work applied to braziers. Trainees learn to count heartbeats between core-pulses to gauge fire-core stability — a technique passed through generations of deep-tunnel keepers. The catechism *what is hoarded is power preserved* serves as governing doctrine.
    
    ## Authority Beyond Fire
    
    The Fire Keepers claim authority over memorial rites in the tunnels, though jurisdictional disputes over specific rites are common enough to be structural. Their influence extends to dictating the language of memorial inscriptions — ordering Remembrancers to amend entries and framing the faction wars as inevitable rather than chosen. A Fire Keeper mandate expanded the Umbra∴go memorial zone by twelve fathoms east, prohibiting all ice-work and fire-draw within the boundary after a previous exception cost three names added to the wall.
    
    Attendance at ceremonies such as the Ritus∴um is enforced by noting absences and excluding non-attendees from fire-core distribution. In a colony where warmth is survival, such exclusion functions as erasure.
    
    Fire Keeper patrols once secured the Berg's corridors against orca raiders, staffed through arrangement with the ☽'shadow Covens' Order. The Covens' inability to continue providing personnel has left those corridors exposed. Under that same arrangement, Fire Keepers served as ceremonial guards at faction political gatherings — stationed at chamber vents during proclamations like sentries dressed as priests.
    
    ## Political and Judicial Role
    
    The Chief Fire Keeper served as appointed prosecutor in the Shadow Parliament tribunal that dissolved the Midnight Claws, a Nightshelf syndicate charged with thirty winters of unsanctioned fire-core diversion. Fire Keeper cryptographers broke the cipher in the Claws' shipping ledger after the syndicate leader's confession. Guard posts at the Glow-Fissure — a corruption site the Claws had controlled for twenty-two winters — were transferred to Fire Keeper authority with a three-day mandate to establish rotation or forfeit the claim. The Fire Keepers adopted the Claws' existing schedule but lacked training for deep-fissure duty; corruption readings at sub-third descent increased measurably after the transfer. The Shadow-Walk Detachment's subsequent reconnaissance of the Glow-Fissure suggests this deterioration is ongoing.
    
    During the succession crisis that fractured the Aurora Stack, the Fire Keepers tightened their grip on forge access, requiring witnessed rationing even for Communion teaching sessions and reassigning penguins who asked questions to the cold-tunnels.
    
    ## Losses and Hazards
    
    The containment failure beneath Terrace Momiou remains their most costly single incident. An experimental fire-core that fused aurora-light with captured flame burned self-sustaining before developing what accounts describe as a hunger — consuming light, heat, and memory from its surroundings. The containment effort was abandoned; the core was sealed behind overlapping faction wards rather than destroyed. Official records list fourteen Fire Keepers lost. The ice-memory in the relevant Foundation stratum records sixteen thermal signatures ceasing in that chamber. Two appear to have been redistributed into the Profun∴lapsum casualty rolls.
    
    Separately, three Fire Keeper smiths were corrupted by the Omega Obelisk — a whale-bone artifact tied to the dead god — before the Wake-Singers claimed custody of it.
    
    ## Present Status
    
    With Shadow-Broker Nyla's confession and the Midnight Claws' dissolution, the Fire Keepers and the ☽'shadow Covens' Order now contest influence over the trade routes and enforcement structures the Claws once monopolized. The Fire Keepers hold the infrastructure. Whether they hold the competence to manage what they have acquired — particularly at the Glow-Fissure — the corruption readings answer more honestly than the Fire Keepers themselves.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771592450708_0", anchor: "the first to touch the wall of the god's heart and feel it pulse", text: "Smoke-oaths degrade. The oldest coherent tunnel-chant fragments I have recovered from comparable strata reference fire-extraction protocols — temperatures, vein-widths, cooling intervals. Not theology. The divine encounter narrative appears in layers roughly four generations younger than the extraction records. They mined first. They decided what they were mining from later.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771592450708_1", anchor: "what is hoarded is power preserved", text: "The Way∴ens exists as direct doctrinal refutation of this sentence. That both ideologies now circulate through the same guild halls means the Nightshelf is arguing with itself about whether survival demands monopoly or distribution — and the fire-core shortage has made the argument lethal rather than theoretical.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771592450708_2", anchor: "corruption readings at sub-third descent increased measurably after the transfer", text: "Three days to establish rotation at a breach-point the Claws spent twenty-two winters learning to manage. That mandate was designed to be failed.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771592450708_3", anchor: "Two appear to have been redistributed into the Profun∴lapsum casualty rolls", text: "Fourteen is a containment-team roster number. Sixteen raises questions about who authorized the experimental core and who was present without sanction. The ice recorded sixteen thermal signatures ceasing — not fourteen signatures and two administrative transfers. Someone moved the dead between reports after the fact. The Profun∴lapsum flooding killed enough penguins that two more vanish into the total without disturbing the count. This is not falsification in the technical sense; the dead are still dead, still counted. But it reshapes the narrative of both incidents simultaneously, and I am reflexively suspicious of any accounting whose primary effect is to make a round number rounder.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771592450708_4", anchor: "reassigning penguins who asked questions to the cold-tunnels", text: "Read this alongside the exclusion from fire-core distribution for missed ceremonies. The Fire Keepers do not imprison. They do not execute. They adjust proximity to warmth. In a colony where a fire-core shortage is measured in days of survival, controlling who stands near the brazier and who is sent to the cold-tunnels is controlling who lives comfortably and who lives provisionally. Every theocracy discovers this mechanism eventually. The Fire Keepers discovered it early and dressed it as logistics.", type: :commentary, display: :full
